.el .ds Aq '
.TH rev-stealth-hermes 1  "rev-stealth-hermes " 
.SH NAME
rev\-stealth\-hermes \- v1.2.0 (P7.3): manage the Hermes plugin scaffold (`install` / `uninstall` / `verify`)
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBrev\-stealth hermes\fR [\fB\-\-output\-format\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIsubcommands\fR>
.SH DESCRIPTION
Manage the Hermes MCP plugin scaffold (P7.3). install copies the bundled scaffold to <prefix>; uninstall removes it; verify checks the required files + (by default) runs a python3 ast.parse syntax probe on __init__.py.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-output\-format\fR \fI<OUTPUT_FORMAT>\fR
Output format for this subcommand: `human` (default) or `json`. Shadows the global `\-\-format` for this invocation. Same value enum as the global flag; the JSON output is documented under `docs/json\-schemas/cli/<subcommand>.output.json`
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
human
.IP \(bu 2
json
.RE
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
rev\-stealth\-hermes\-install(1)
Install the Hermes plugin scaffold into `<prefix>`
.TP
rev\-stealth\-hermes\-uninstall(1)
Remove a previously installed Hermes plugin
.TP
rev\-stealth\-hermes\-verify(1)
Verify a Hermes plugin install on disk
.SH EXTRA
EXAMPLES:
  $ rev\-stealth hermes install
  $ rev\-stealth hermes verify
  $ rev\-stealth hermes uninstall \-\-prefix /opt/hermes/plugins/rev\-scraping\-mcp

EXIT CODES:
  0  Ok               Action completed.
  1  UserError        Bad \-\-prefix / install conflict (use \-\-force).
  3  PermanentError   Scaffold IO failure / python3 syntax check failed.

ENV:
  (none consumed directly; respects HOME for default \-\-prefix.)
